-- infrastructure/scripts/seed-local-d1.sql
--
-- Local-dev seed data (ROADMAP.md Milestone A.1, spec §20 Phase 0 step 5):
-- 20 companies with realistic, sanitized sources/jobs/signals so
-- GET /api/v1/signals and related routes return real rows against local
-- D1 without needing a live ATS fetch. "Sanitized" per A.1's own
-- instruction: no real company postings copy-pasted -- every company,
-- domain, and job posting below is synthesized in the shape real ones
-- take (same convention as packages/adapters/src/fixtures/
-- greenhouse-board.json's "examplecorp"), all company domains use the
-- reserved .example TLD (RFC 2606) so nothing here resolves to a real site.
--
-- Run: wrangler d1 execute hiring-signals --local \
--        --file=infrastructure/scripts/seed-local-d1.sql
--      (from apps/api/, where wrangler.toml's d1_databases binding lives)
--
-- Shape, so this seed exercises what the read-path repos and routes
-- actually query:
--   - 20 companies, one source each, spread across all 11 ATS providers.
--   - 1 successful source_runs row per source (status='success'), all
--     within the last few hours, so source-health scripts (Milestone D)
--     have something realistic to report once written.
--   - 3 jobs per company (60 total) spanning different role_primary
--     categories and location_mode values (remote/hybrid/onsite, US/DE/GB)
--     so the roles/locationMode/country facet filters (facets-repo.ts,
--     signals-repo.ts EXISTS clauses) have real variety to filter against.
--     All classification_confidence >= 0.80 (auto-classified, spec §6.2
--     step 6) with classification_version='v1'.
--   - 1 job_observations row per job, keyed to its source_run -- exercises
--     idx_job_observations_idempotency (migration 0004) without violating
--     it (one observation per (job, run) pair here, as a real run would
--     produce).
--   - 1 active `new_job` signal per company (20 total, spec §20 Phase 1's
--     "new_job only for v1" build order), anchored to each company's most
--     recently posted job, with score computed from spec §7.2's formula
--     (freshness decay dominant since v1 doesn't have volume/acceleration
--     baselines yet -- same v1 simplification signals-write-repo.ts's
--     header comment will need to document once Milestone C lands) and
--     one signal_evidence row per signal.
--   - first_detected_at/last_detected_at values are all within the last
--     30 days so listSignals' default observedSince window (signals-
--     repo.ts) returns them without extra query params.
--
-- Idempotent re-runs: this file does not attempt upsert semantics (no
-- ON CONFLICT) -- re-running it against a DB that already has this seed
-- will fail on the UNIQUE(provider, board_token) / UNIQUE(source_id,
-- external_job_id) constraints. That's intentional: local dev resets via
-- `rm -rf .wrangler/state/v3/d1` + re-applying migrations 0001-0004 is
-- the supported way to get a clean slate, not a second seed run on top
-- of the first.







